 You must implement the following function 
Function name: calculate_pi
Parameters: int argc, char **argv
Return type: int

Brief description:
Estimates the value of π using the Monte Carlo simulation method with OpenMP parallelization. The number of iterations N is calculated as 256 × 256 × the command-line input. For each iteration, it generates a random point (x, y) in the unit square and checks if it lies inside the unit circle. A parallel for-loop with reduction accumulates the count of points inside the circle. It then computes π as 4 * (points inside) / N, calculates the relative error compared to the actual value of π (acos(-1)), and measures the total execution time in milliseconds. The results are printed to the console.

code_gens.code:
#include <omp.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

#define PI 3.14159265358979323846
#define MAX_ITERATIONS 256 * 256

double calculate_pi(int argc, char **argv) {
    int N = atoi(argv[1]);
    double sum_inside_circle = 0.0;
    double total_time = 0.0;
    double relative_error;

    double x, y;
    double pi_estimate;
    double actual_pi = acos(-1);

    double start_time = omp_get_wtime();
    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        #pragma omp parallel for reduction(+: sum_inside_circle) private(x, y)
        for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
            x = rand() / ((double)RAND_MAX + 1);
            y = rand() / ((double)RAND_MAX + 1);
            if (x * x + y * y <= 1) {
                sum_inside_circle++;
            }
        }
    }
    total_time = omp_get_wtime() - start_time;

    pi_estimate = 4 * sum_inside_circle / N;
    relative_error = fabs(pi_estimate - actual_pi) / actual_pi;

    printf("Estimated Pi: %.10f\n", pi_estimate);
    printf("Relative Error: %.10f\n", relative_error);
    printf("Total Execution Time: %.6f ms\n", total_time * 1000);

    return 0;
}

